2026-11-03 11:56:53,903 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='How are the refunds made if policy is cancelled in cooling off period?' Response="Full refund of premiums paid, less non-refundable government charges, taxes and levies, unless you've made a claim, exercised a policy right/power, or the policy has ended. The request must go through your intermediary. [Page 5]\n\nAny agency fee added to the premium is also refunded. [Page 58]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:5', 0.52), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:58', 0.42)] time_taken=2.704126700060442 input_tokens=1989 output_tokens=144
2026-11-03 11:56:57,962 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='What is an Excess and how does it apply to my policy?' Response="An **excess** is the first amount of each claim that you (or the person claiming) must pay. [Page 64] It is not an additional fee, but the uninsured first portion of a covered loss. [Page 13]\n\n**How it applies to your policy:**\n- An excess may apply to each available cover. [Page 13]\n- Depending on the claim, one or more of these may apply: basic, undeclared young driver, undeclared inexperienced driver, or undeclared driver history excess. [Page 13]\n- Amounts are shown on your policy schedule or in the PDS. [Page 13], [Page 64]\n- In some situations, no excess is payable. [Page 13]\n- If one applies, you pay it to the insurer or a preferred repairer when requested, no later than when your claim is being finalised. [Page 13]\n- Don't accept payment of any excess from anyone without the insurer's prior consent. [Page 13]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:13', 0.52), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:64', 0.47)] time_taken=4.05795509996824 input_tokens=1863 output_tokens=350
