2026-11-03 11:57:05,732 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='How much of my premium is refunded if I cancel inside versus outside the cooling-off period?' Response="**Inside the cooling-off period (30 days):** Full refund of premiums paid, less non-refundable government charges, taxes and levies, unless you've made a claim, exercised a policy right or power, or the policy has ended. Requests go through your intermediary. [Page 5]\n\n**Outside the cooling-off period:** A proportion of the premium (and any roadside assistance fees) for the unexpired period of insurance, less non-refundable government charges, taxes and levies. [Page 58]\n\n**Agency fees:** Refunded only if you cancel within the cooling-off period or the cancellation is effective from the start of the period of insurance. [Page 58]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:5', 0.46), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:58', 0.41)] time_taken=3.1636518000159413 input_tokens=1996 output_tokens=255
2026-11-03 11:57:10,450 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='What is the difference between New-for-old replacement and Lifetime new-for-old replacement after a total loss?' Response="**Differences shown in the document:**\n\n- **Availability:** Lifetime new-for-old replacement applies only to Comprehensive Plus cover. New-for-old replacement applies to both Comprehensive Plus and Comprehensive cover. [Page 33]\n- **Priority:** Under Comprehensive Plus, if you're eligible for Lifetime new-for-old replacement, you can't claim New-for-old replacement. [Page 37]\n\n**New-for-old replacement conditions:** [Page 37]\n- Vehicle was bought new or ex-demonstration from the manufacturer or a licensed dealer.\n- At total loss, it was under 3 years since first registration and had travelled under 70,000 km.\n- Any finance company with an interest has given written consent.\n\nThe document doesn't give the conditions for Lifetime new-for-old replacement." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:33', 0.51), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:37', 0.5)] time_taken=4.716831099940464 input_tokens=1365 output_tokens=420
2026-11-03 11:57:14,247 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='Which excesses can apply to a claim, and when does the undeclared young driver excess apply?' Response="**Excesses that may apply [Page 13]:**\n- Basic excess\n- Undeclared young driver excess\n- Undeclared inexperienced driver excess\n- Undeclared driver history excess\n\n**Undeclared young driver excess applies when the driver [Page 14]:**\n- is under 25; and\n- is not a named driver on the policy schedule.\n\nIt is payable in addition to the basic excess.\n\n**It does not apply when [Page 14]:**\n- the basic excess isn't payable;\n- the claim is only for glass damage, damage while parked by another vehicle (not caused by your vehicle's user), theft, attempted theft, vandalism, malicious damage, or hail, storm, flood or fire;\n- the driver was an accompanied learner, or a car park/valet attendant or repairer/servicer; or\n- you prove you didn't consent to them driving." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:14', 0.56), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:13', 0.54)] time_taken=3.7960332999937236 input_tokens=1998 output_tokens=329
2026-11-03 11:57:18,532 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query="How is my vehicle's value worked out under agreed value versus market value?" Response="**Agreed value:** The vehicle sum insured on your policy schedule, plus the value of any non-standard accessories or modifications, unless automatically covered under 'Accessories, spare parts and tools'. [Page 11] [Page 64]\n\n**Market value:** Assessed at claim time, considering:\n- Vehicle's condition and age at the incident\n- Non-standard accessories/modifications specified on your policy schedule\n- Local market prices for similar vehicles\n- Motor industry valuation guides [Page 11]\n\nIt's the cost to replace your vehicle with one of the same make, model, age and condition immediately before the loss. It includes registration and CTP but excludes stamp duty transfer, dealer warranty costs and transfer fees. [Page 64]\n\nValues exclude GST unless otherwise stated. [Page 11]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:11', 0.58), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:64', 0.51)] time_taken=4.283944200025871 input_tokens=2055 output_tokens=330
2026-11-03 11:57:22,908 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query="Can I choose my own repairer, and what happens if you don't agree with my repairer's quote?" Response="**Choosing your repairer:**\n- Only if your policy schedule includes the **'Choice of repairer' option**; you must provide the repairer's quote for assessment. [Page 16]\n- Without it, a nearby preferred repairer is arranged. [Page 16]\n\n**If the quote isn't agreed:**\n- The insurer pays you the **reasonable cost of repairs** instead (see 'Choice of repairer' under 'Optional covers' on page 55). [Page 18]\n- This is based on your repairer's quote, a preferred repairer's quote, an assessor's report and your vehicle's location. [Page 18]\n- Your vehicle may be moved, at the insurer's expense, for assessment or another quote. [Page 18]\n- You then organise the repairs and pay the applicable excess. [Page 18]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:18', 0.59), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:16', 0.58)] time_taken=4.3753849000204355 input_tokens=2255 output_tokens=323
2026-11-03 11:57:26,903 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='Does this policy include home and contents insurance?' Response="The document doesn't mention home and contents insurance. It only covers personal items, clothing and tools of trade that are damaged in an accident or fire involving your vehicle, stolen from your locked vehicle, or stolen when your vehicle is stolen. This is limited to $1,000 (Comprehensive) or $2,000 (Comprehensive Plus) per incident [Page 51]." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:51', 0.38), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:6', 0.37)] time_taken=3.9939337999094278 input_tokens=1885 output_tokens=295
