2026-11-03 12:40:43,707 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='How much of my premium is refunded if I cancel inside versus outside the cooling-off period?' Response="**Inside cooling-off (30 days):** Full refund of premiums paid, less non-refundable government charges, taxes and levies, unless you've made a claim, exercised a policy right, or the policy has ended [Page 5].\n\n**Outside cooling-off:** Proportional refund of premium (and roadside assistance fees, if applicable) for the unexpired period, less non-refundable government charges, taxes and levies [Page 58].\n\n**Agency fees:** Refunded only if cancelled within cooling-off or effective from the start of the insurance period [Page 58]." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:5', 0.46), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:58', 0.41)] time_taken=3.654658399987966 input_tokens=1996 output_tokens=238
2026-11-03 12:40:48,588 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='What is the difference between New-for-old replacement and Lifetime new-for-old replacement after a total loss?' Response="**Availability:**\n- **New-for-old replacement:** Comprehensive Plus and Comprehensive cover. [Page 33]\n- **Lifetime new-for-old replacement:** Comprehensive Plus cover only. [Page 33]\n\n**New-for-old conditions:** The vehicle must have been bought new (or ex-demo) from the manufacturer or a licensed dealer, be under 3 years from original registration, have travelled under 70,000kms, and have written consent from any finance company. [Page 37]\n\n**Overlap:** Under Comprehensive Plus, if you're eligible for Lifetime new-for-old, you can't claim New-for-old. [Page 37]\n\nThe document doesn't describe Lifetime new-for-old's own conditions or benefits." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:33', 0.51), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:37', 0.51)] time_taken=4.880577699979767 input_tokens=1365 output_tokens=407
2026-11-03 12:40:54,082 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='Which excesses can apply to a claim, and when does the undeclared young driver excess apply?' Response='**Excesses that may apply:** [Page 13]\n- Basic excess\n- Undeclared young driver excess\n- Undeclared inexperienced driver excess\n- Undeclared driver history excess\n\n**Undeclared young driver excess applies when the driver** (of your vehicle or substitute vehicle) at the time of the incident: [Page 14]\n- is under 25, and\n- is not a named driver on your policy schedule.\n\nIt is payable in addition to the basic excess. [Page 14]\n\n**It does not apply when:** [Page 14]\n- the basic excess is not payable;\n- the claim is only for windscreen, window, mirror or sunscreen glass;\n- the claim is for damage by another vehicle while yours was parked, not caused or contributed to by any user of your vehicle;\n- the claim is for theft, attempted theft, vandalism or malicious damage;\n- the claim is for hail, storm, flood or fire damage;\n- the driver was a learner accompanied by a full unrestricted Australian licence holder;\n- the driver was a car park or valet attendant on duty, or your vehicle was being repaired or serviced; or\n- you prove you did not consent to that person driving.' chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:14', 0.56), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:13', 0.54)] time_taken=5.492832400137559 input_tokens=1998 output_tokens=438
2026-11-03 12:40:59,571 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query="How is my vehicle's value worked out under agreed value versus market value?" Response="**Agreed value** [Page 11]:\n- Vehicle sum insured on your policy schedule; plus\n- Value of non-standard accessories/modifications, unless automatically covered under 'Accessories, spare parts and tools'.\n\n**Market value** [Page 11] is assessed at claim time, considering:\n- Vehicle's condition and age at the incident\n- Non-standard accessories/modifications specified on your schedule\n- Local market prices for similar vehicles\n- Motor industry valuation guides\n\nIt's the cost to replace your vehicle with one of the same make, model, age and condition immediately before the loss. It includes registration and CTP, but excludes stamp duty transfer, dealer warranty costs and transfer fees [Page 64].\n\n**Both** [Page 11]:\n- Exclude GST unless otherwise stated.\n- Include standard manufacturer accessories." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:11', 0.59), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:64', 0.51)] time_taken=5.487595799844712 input_tokens=2055 output_tokens=334
2026-11-03 12:41:03,525 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query="Can I choose my own repairer, and what happens if you don't agree with my repairer's quote?" Response="**Choosing your repairer:** Only if your policy schedule includes the ‘Choice of repairer’ option. You can then use a licensed repairer of your choice, but must provide their quote for assessment. Without this option, a preferred repairer will be arranged [Page 16].\n\n**If the quote isn't agreed:** The insurer may pay you the reasonable cost of repairs instead of authorising them [Page 16][Page 18]. This cost is based on:\n- your repairer’s quote\n- a preferred repairer’s quote\n- assessor reports\n- your vehicle’s location\n\nYour vehicle may be moved at their expense for assessment or another quote. You must then organise the repairs yourself and pay the excess [Page 18]." chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:18', 0.59), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:16', 0.58)] time_taken=3.95190059999004 input_tokens=2255 output_tokens=287
2026-11-03 12:41:08,130 INFO rag_from_scratch_v1.processing.query Query='Does this policy include home and contents insurance?' Response="No, the document doesn't mention home and contents insurance. It is a vehicle policy that covers personal items only when they are:\n\n- damaged in an accident or fire involving your vehicle,\n- stolen from your locked vehicle, or\n- stolen when your vehicle is stolen.\n\nLimits are $1,000 (Comprehensive) or $2,000 (Comprehensive Plus) per incident. [Page 51]" chunk=[('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:51', 0.38), ('Motor_Insurance_Comprehensive:page:6', 0.37)] time_taken=4.602219299878925 input_tokens=1885 output_tokens=314
